# Kit + user Cursor rules

User global rules in `~/.cursor/rules/` **win on conflict**. The kit supplements them;
it does not replace them.

## Before loading kit guidelines

1. Read `~/.cursor/kit-user-rules.manifest.json` — it carries `kit_root`, the absolute
   path every kit doc resolves against.
2. **Do not read** files listed in `skip_kit_guidelines` — user rules already cover
   those topics.
3. **Always read** every path in `always_load_kit_guidelines_resolved` (absolute paths
   under `kit_root`). Applies in every project — no project install required.
4. Load `optional_kit_guidelines` only when the task needs them and no user rule applies.

Global rules `kit-comprehension.mdc` and this file apply to all repos in the **Cursor
IDE**. The Cursor CLI (`agent` binary) does not read `~/.cursor/rules/` — it needs a
project install (`./scripts/kit install --target=cursor --project`) per repo.

Regenerate the manifest after adding or renaming user rules:

```text
./scripts/kit sync-rules
```

Optional local overrides: `~/.cursor/kit-user-rules.local.yaml` — documented in
`docs/cursor-user-rules.md` in the kit tree.
